          "en": "<p>If $X\\ge0$, $E[X]&lt;\\infty$, and $a&gt;0$, Markov's inequality gives an upper bound:</p>$$P(X\\ge a)\\le\\frac{E[X]}a$$<div class=\"example-box\"><h4>Example</h4><p>If a nonnegative waiting time has mean 5 minutes, the probability of waiting at least 20 minutes is at most $5/20=0.25$. This is a bound, not the exact probability, and it may be loose.</p></div>",
